<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2014/Phillips-Farm.jpg" alt="A small landscape painting featuring shrubs sitting on a bank." width="450" height="364" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Phillips Farm. 8x10 oil on linen panel. 2014.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Another small painting that I worked on over the weekend. &nbsp;I've been sitting on some photos I took at Waterford for a couple of years now and finally decided to use some of them as the basis for a painting. &nbsp;I pushed the treeline high up in the painting and led the eye in by manipulating temperatures and colors in the foreground and middleground.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">One of my goals was to keep the brush work and paint application as loose as possible so I painted directly on top of a burnt umber/yellow ochre imprimatura.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">This is one of the scenes that you see when you take the footpath that starts behind the mill and follow it for a quarter mile or so. &nbsp;It feels very remote back there and I'm always on the lookout for bears and angry raccoons.</p>